    Revert the synchronous-tracing thread equalizer that kills setitimer under KVM
    
    [hermit2, cleanup-3, claude-opus-5, devbig014, role=impl]
    
    Reverts the three lines added to init_sync_file_tracing() by 1d9c9094de
    "Preserve the initial thread identity in synchronous tracing"
    (https://github.com/rrnewton/hermit/pull/2945), which made
    c-programs/setitimer-determinism (verify/kvm) fail.
    
    The helper those lines call is, in full:
    
        fn equalize_tracing_thread_number() {
            // Create an extra, pointless thread just so that our thread number
            // starts at the same DetTid "3" that `init_file_tracing` does.
            std::thread::spawn(|| {}).join().unwrap();
        }
    
    so the synchronous verification-logging path spawned and joined a HOST THREAD
    during init. Under KVM with an interval timer the sandbox is then killed by
    SIGALRM: "sandbox failed during Run1: Signaled { signal: 14, core_dumped:
    false }; no guest disposition or comparison was returned". ptrace is unaffected.
    
    LOCATED BY BISECT, CONFIRMED BY REVERT. Bisect over the 112 commits between
    fe4108174265 (last observed pass, 2026-09-16 17:47) and ebc2a64b4f18 converged
    in 7 probes with zero untestable. A bisect result is a correlation until the
    revert is tried, so it was tried, at current main 8255986391:
    
        before   FAIL c-programs/setitimer-determinism (verify/kvm)
                 PASS c-programs/setitimer-determinism (verify/ptrace)
        after    PASS c-programs/setitimer-determinism (verify/kvm)
                 PASS c-programs/setitimer-determinism (verify/ptrace)
    
    ⚠️ THIS REVERT REINTRODUCES A REAL MISMATCH AND THE COST IS NAMED RATHER THAN
    DISCOVERED LATER. The three lines had a legitimate purpose: aligning the initial
    DetTid baseline for synchronous verification logging with the baseline
    init_file_tracing produces. Removing them restores that misalignment, which is
    determinism-relevant. There is no test on either side -- the helper has three
    call sites and zero tests -- so nothing in the suite guards 2945's intent, and
    nothing will go red to remind anyone.
    
    The obligation is tracked rather than left to memory:
    TaskGraph restore-the-dettid-alignment-without-spawning-a-host-thread (OPEN).
    
    The defect is in the MECHANISM, not the goal. Burning a DetTid by spawning a
    host thread perturbs signal and timer delivery in the KVM sandbox; achieving the
    same alignment without spawning a thread would satisfy both. That change belongs
    in tracing init on the determinism path and should be made deliberately, not as
    part of a revert.
    
    Trade being made, explicitly: a known, measured blocker on
    e2e.manifest_c_programs -- which gates the reverie pin bump,
    https://github.com/rrnewton/hermit/pull/3066 and a third landing -- for a named
    and tracked identity mismatch. Not for silence.
    
    No assertion, tolerance, cell or case was weakened, retired or deleted. The cell
    is correct and it caught a real defect.

